From: Paige Hearn <hearnpaige01>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 18:47:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] baikal: explicit Sia/Blake2b work fill and AlphaPool notes

Sia/Decred in baikal_update_work set count = 0 then fell through
the default case to count = 4. That happens to keep boards fed,
but a later break would starve Blake2b work.

- Give ALGO_SIA and ALGO_DECRED an explicit prefill of 4 jobs
- Keep warehouse clock at BAIKAL_CLK_DEF (400); do not raise it here
- AlphaPool Knots BLAKE2b: use port 7777 for Sia-firmware ASICs
  (BK-B, A3, iBeLink). Port 5555 is Goldshell-style.

Applies on top of Blakestream-GaintB patches 0001-0011, against
cod3gen/sgminer-baikal (dev). Line numbers may need fuzz.
---
 driver-baikalu.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/driver-baikalu.c b/driver-baikalu.c
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/driver-baikalu.c
+++ b/driver-baikalu.c
@@ -871,16 +871,22 @@ static void baikal_update_work(struct cgpu_info *baikal)
     if (baikal->miner_id == 0) {
         switch(baikal->algorithm.type) {
         case ALGO_CRYPTONIGHT:
         case ALGO_CRYPTONIGHT_LITE:
             count = 1;
             break;
         case ALGO_SIA:
         case ALGO_DECRED:
-            count = 0;
+            /* Sia/Blake2b and Decred: keep the work FIFO primed.
+             * Upstream set count = 0 and fell through to default (4).
+             * Make that explicit so a future break cannot starve boards.
+             * AlphaPool BTCB2b: usN.alphapool.tech:7777 for this firmware. */
+            count = 4;
+            break;
         default:
             count = 4;
+            break;
         }
 
         for (i = 0; i < info->miner_count; i++) {
             miner = &info->miners[i];
